// Detection: Large Upload to Unsanctioned Cloud Storage Domain
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1567.002 (Exfiltration Over Web Service: Exfiltration to Cloud Storage)
// Log source: Microsoft Defender XDR — DeviceNetworkEvents
//
// What it detects:
//   A device sending an unusually large volume of outbound traffic to
//   personal cloud storage / file-sharing domains (Mega, Dropbox
//   personal, MediaFire, transfer.sh, etc.) that are not on the
//   organization's sanctioned SaaS list.
//
// Why it matters:
//   Personal file-sharing sites are a favorite exfiltration channel
//   because they use standard HTTPS on 443 and are rarely blocked
//   outright (unlike raw FTP or unusual ports), letting traffic blend
//   in with normal web browsing. Volume-based detection on a curated
//   domain list catches this without needing DLP content inspection.
//
// False positive considerations:
//   - Maintain the UnsanctionedDomains list actively — sanctioned
//     corporate storage (your official OneDrive/SharePoint/Box tenant)
//     should never appear here, and the list will need periodic updates
//     as new services emerge.
//   - Marketing/creative teams legitimately uploading large media files
//     to approved external partners can trigger this; pair with a
//     business-context allowlist per department if false positives are
//     high.
//   - Bytes-sent thresholds should be tuned to your environment's
//     typical upload baseline — the 100MB default below is a starting
//     point, not a universal constant.

let UnsanctionedDomains = dynamic([
    "mega.nz", "mediafire.com", "transfer.sh", "wetransfer.com",
    "sendspace.com", "gofile.io", "anonfiles.com"
]);
let MinBytesSent = 100000000; // 100 MB
DeviceNetworkEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(1d)
| where ActionType == "ConnectionSuccess"
| where RemoteUrl has_any (UnsanctionedDomains)
| summarize TotalBytesSent = sum(todouble(column_ifexists("SentBytes", 0))), ConnectionCount = count()
    by DeviceName, RemoteUrl, InitiatingProcessAccountName
| where TotalBytesSent >= MinBytesSent
| order by TotalBytesSent desc
